    {
      "heading": "Function notation",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Instead of y equals two x plus 1, we write f of x equals two x plus 1.",
          "write": "f(x) = 2x + 1"
        },
        {
          "say": "f of 3 means the output when the input is 3.",
          "write": "f(3) = 2(3) + 1 = 7",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 260,
            "alt": "A function machine",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 200,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 160,
                "h": 100,
                "fill": "purple",
                "label": "f(x) = 2x + 1"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 80,
                "y": 148,
                "text": "3",
                "size": 30,
                "color": "blue",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 110,
                "y": 140,
                "x2": 195,
                "y2": 140,
                "color": "blue"
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 365,
                "y": 140,
                "x2": 450,
                "y2": 140,
                "color": "orange",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 490,
                "y": 148,
                "text": "7",
                "size": 30,
                "color": "orange",
                "change": "add",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "So the point 3, 7 is on the graph.",
          "write": "(3, 7)"
        },
        {
          "say": "f of x does not mean f times x.",
          "write": "f(3) ≠ f × 3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Substituting",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Let f of x be x squared minus three x plus 2.",
          "write": "f(x) = x² − 3x + 2"
        },
        {
          "say": "f of 4. Replace every x with 4. You get 6.",
          "write": "f(4) = 16 − 12 + 2 = 6"
        },
        {
          "say": "f of minus 1. Use brackets to keep the signs right.",
          "write": "f(−1) = 1 + 3 + 2 = 6"
        },
        {
          "say": "A letter can be an input too. Replace x with a.",
          "write": "f(a) = a² − 3a + 2"
        },
        {
          "say": "With an expression, use brackets. f of x plus 3 needs x plus 3, all squared.",
          "write": "f(x+3) = (x+3)² − 3(x+3) + 2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Solving f(x) = a number",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Solve f of x equals 11, when f of x is 5 minus two x.",
          "write": "5 − 2x = 11"
        },
        {
          "say": "Now we know the output. We want the input.",
          "write": "output 11 → input ?",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 260,
            "alt": "A function machine",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 200,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 160,
                "h": 100,
                "fill": "purple",
                "label": "f(x) = 2x + 1"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 80,
                "y": 148,
                "text": "?",
                "size": 30,
                "color": "blue",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 110,
                "y": 140,
                "x2": 195,
                "y2": 140,
                "color": "blue"
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 365,
                "y": 140,
                "x2": 450,
                "y2": 140,
                "color": "orange",
                "change": "highlight"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 490,
                "y": 148,
                "text": "11",
                "size": 30,
                "color": "orange",
                "change": "highlight",
                "bold": true
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Subtract 5 from both sides.",
          "write": "−2x = 6"
        },
        {
          "say": "Divide by minus 2. x is minus 3.",
          "write": "x = −3"
        },
        {
          "say": "Check. f of minus 3 is 5 plus 6, which is 11.",
          "write": "f(−3) = 11 ✓"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Domain and range",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "The domain is the x-values you can put in.",
          "write": "domain: inputs (x)"
        },
        {
          "say": "The range is the y-values that come out.",
          "write": "range: outputs (y)"
        },
        {
          "say": "You can't divide by zero. One over x minus 2 needs x not equal to 2.",
